text:
nina: Heads-up: found a new redaction gap triggered by client-side retries in the Java SDK. When the retry middleware replays requests, logs from retry attempts sometimes include raw payloads even though Node sampleapp is fine. Feels like an SDK parity issue between Java (uses MDC) and Node (uses ALS).

harry: interesting. Did you repro with our java-sampleapp? which retry config?

nina: repro steps in /scripts/repro-retry.sh. java-sampleapp v0.7.2, retry policy exponential with maxAttempts=3. When retries occur we see logs like:```
2026-06-20T11:10:01Z INFO reqid=jd-9 route=/v1/generate attempt=1 payload={"email":"a@ex.com"}
2026-06-20T11:10:02Z INFO reqid=jd-9 route=/v1/generate attempt=2 payload={"email":"a@ex.com"}
2026-06-20T11:10:02Z DEBUG reqid=jd-9 redactor=skipped payload={"phone":"+1400"}
```

sam: the pattern suggests MDC is preserved across retries but redactor checks a per-request marker that is only set on initial dispatch. In Node we attach reqid via ALS per attempt. In Java we stash reqid in MDC at client creation time, not per attempt.

mona: code snippet from our Java retry wrapper:```java
void send(Request r){
  MDC.put("reqid", baseReqid);
  for (int i=1;i<=max;i++){
    try{ transport.send(r); break;}catch(e){ //retry }
  }
}
```

harry: so MDC.put is called once; attempts reuse same reqid and redactor sees attempt>1 and skips redaction? why would redactor skip on retries?

nina: our redactor has heuristic to skip heavy scrubbing for non-first attempts to avoid double-cost for idempotent replays (we thought payloads already scrubbed upstream). That heuristic is wrong if retries re-log the original payload.

sam: agreed. two fixes: 1) make redactor stateless and always scrub logs, or 2) update SDKs to mark attempts as scrubbed before sending out and ensure MDC/ALS are per-attempt so the marker flow is consistent. For parity, prefer per-attempt context (Java: put MDC inside attempt loop) and keep redactor idempotent.

mona: minimal patch: move MDC.put inside the retry loop and set attempt tag:```java
for(...){
  MDC.put("reqid", reqid + "-a"+attempt);
  MDC.put("attempt", String.valueOf(attempt));
  transport.send(r);
}
```

nina: opened PR #508 to update java-sampleapp and SDK retry wrapper, plus change redactor to be idempotent (safe to run multiple times). Added repro harness and an integ test that forces 3 retries and asserts no raw email/phone in any log line.

harry: small addition: emit metric retry_redaction_bypass when redactor sees skipped on attempt>1 so Optimize can pick it up. Also add a cross-SDK test in our sampleapps matrix to assert parity.

sam: also add a lint rule in java-sdk to warn on putting reqid at client scope; require it be set per attempt or use our SDK helper attachReqidForAttempt().

mona: temporary mitigation: set LOG_LEVEL=info for java-sampleapp on Dedicated until patch lands: `kubectl set env deploy/java-sampleapp LOG_LEVEL=info -n dedicated`

telemetry-bot: java-sampleapp/staging v0.7.2 -> deploy triggered :hourglass_flowing_sand: (build 1160)

ci-bot: quick smoke on staging passed (no retries during smoke).

nina: thanks team. tagging @sam @harry for reviews. Will follow up with backport plan for 0.7.x and a changelog entry about retry/redaction parity.

sam: will review PR today. Great catch, nina. :thumbsup:
